# Purpose
This document describes only La Caracola backend-specific behavior.
Generic engineering rules: [Tech Doc](./tech-doc.mdc).
Product behavior: [Business Doc](./business-doc.mdc).
Data model: [Specific Data Model](./specific-data-model.md).

# Actual architecture
- Monolite Laravel MVC con Blade server-rendered.
- No separate public API: AJAX on web endpoints.
- Admin area in the same codebase, protected by `auth`.
- Global locale middleware on web stack: `ResolveLocaleFromRoute` (see `bootstrap/app.php`).

# Routing and HTTP contracts
- Public routes are locale-prefixed in `routes/web.php` with slugs from `config/routes.php`.
- Admin routes are in `routes/admin.php`, loaded by `bootstrap/app.php` inside `web` middleware.
- Admin login is separate (`/admin/login`), logout is `/logout`.

### SEO discovery endpoints
- `GET /sitemap.xml` is generated dynamically from the registered localized `GET` routes.
  Routes with dynamic parameters, non-public methods, and booking thank-you pages are excluded.
- New public localized `GET` pages are included automatically when their route is registered in
  the locale groups. Verify the sitemap when adding or changing public routes.
- `public/robots.txt` must keep crawling enabled for the general user agent and must reference
  `https://lacaracolaandora.com/sitemap.xml` with a `Sitemap` directive.
- Token-based, transactional, admin, and form-submission endpoints must not be added to the sitemap.

### Hreflang metadata
- The shared public layout generates `hreflang` links only for the equivalent localized route currently being viewed.
- Locale names and localized slugs come from `config/routes.php`; do not duplicate the supported-locale list in SEO code.
- `x-default` points to the Italian equivalent of the current public page.
- Thank-you, token-based, admin, and form-submission routes do not receive hreflang metadata.
- When adding or removing a locale, update `config/routes.php` and all translated public slugs, then verify hreflang tests and the sitemap.

## Public online check-in
- `GET /check-in/{token}` renders the token-based guest form.
- `POST /check-in/{token}/edit` explicitly invalidates a completed check-in and
  returns the guest to the editable form; it is called only after the guest
  confirms the warning in the UI.
- `POST /check-in/{token}/confirm` validates the submitted guest data, persists
  all guest records, and sets `checkin_completed_at` in one database transaction.
  After a successful confirmation it sends `CheckinCompletedMail` to the guest,
  with the owner in BCC; a mail transport failure is logged without undoing the
  completed check-in.
- Validation failures redirect to the check-in page with errors and old input;
  persistence failures roll back the transaction, log the exception, and retain
  the submitted input for retry.
- There is no separate public save endpoint: confirmation is the only operation
  that submits the guest form.

## Critical operational endpoints
- Public quote endpoint: `POST /{locale}/{availability-slug}/quote`
  - valid input: `checkin`, `checkout`
  - JSON output: `available`, `total_cents` plus technical breakdown
- Availability request endpoint: `POST /{locale}/{availability-slug}`
  - supports JSON and form submit
  - requires `accepted_terms` (House Rules + Short-Term Tourist Lease Agreement consent); validated server-side even though the submit button is also disabled client-side until checked
  - rejects requests where `adults + children` exceeds `config('apartment.specs.beds')`; infants and pets are excluded from this capacity check
  - persists a `BookingRequest` record (contact/stay data + `terms_accepted_at`, `ip_address`, `user_agent`) as legal proof of consent — direct/private bookings are never anonymous leads
  - sends owner email (`BookingRequestMail`, states the guest's consent + timestamp), with non-blocking fallback on mail errors
  - sends guest email (`BookingRequestPendingMail`) clarifying the booking is NOT yet confirmed
- Terms page: `GET /{locale}/{terms-slug}` — publishes the short-term tourist lease agreement text (`config('apartment.terms')` + `app.terms_*` lang keys), same pattern as the House Rules page
- Booking confirmation email (admin, manual trigger): `POST /admin/prenotazioni/{id}/send-confirmation` (requires `manage_bookings`)
  - Sends `BookingConfirmedMail` to the booking's guest with payment instructions from the enabled `host_owner` user, a 48h payment deadline, and the free-cancellation deadline (`checkin` − `apartment.payment.free_cancellation_days`, omitted once elapsed)
  - BCCs the owner (`config('apartment.email')`) and includes the guest name plus configured check-in/check-out times in the stay summary
  - Also sends the Italian-only `BookingHostKeeperMail` to all users with the `host_keeper` role, BCCing the owner and including the guest's phone/email when present, guest counts, parking, cleaning and linen service costs, but never the guest price
  - The booking detail page exposes protected GET previews for the guest confirmation, host keeper summary, payment-received, check-in reminder, and guest review request emails; it also exposes direct links to the public check-in and review forms for testing while their guest tokens are active. Email previews render the same Mailable HTML without sending
  - The host owner tax code for the receipt comes from the same enabled `host_owner`; sending is blocked when no payment-enabled host owner exists. Host owners edit their own payment profile at `/admin/impostazioni/profilo-pagamenti`; super admins edit it in user management.
  - Sets `Booking.confirmation_sent_at`; the admin UI warns before resending if already sent
  - No automated cancellation job if unpaid after 48h — the owner cancels manually via the existing `cancel` action
- Payment received email (admin, manual trigger): `POST /admin/prenotazioni/{id}/send-payment-received` (requires `manage_bookings`)
  - Sends `BookingPaymentReceivedMail` only to the guest, with `config('apartment.email')` in BCC
  - Includes booking summary, prominent online check-in link, configured host keeper names/emails, house address, and Google Maps/Apple Maps/OpenStreetMap links
  - After a successful send, sets `income_paid = true`, stores `income_paid_at` as today, and updates `Booking.payment_received_sent_at`; resends are allowed after a browser confirmation
- Check-in reminder email (admin or scheduled): the manual endpoint and `checkin:send-reminders` both update `Booking.checkin_reminder_sent_at` after a successful send; the timestamp represents the last manual or automatic send. The scheduled command sends only when `Booking.checkin_reminder_enabled` is true; the manual action remains available regardless of this setting.
- Completed online check-in email (`CheckinCompletedMail`): sent automatically to the guest after
  `POST /check-in/{token}/confirm` succeeds. It confirms that the online check-in is complete,
  repeats the host keeper contact, house address and map links, free-cancellation deadline, and
  accepted house rules/lease links, and BCCs `config('apartment.email')`.
- Telegram webhook: `POST /api/telegram/webhook/{secret}` (stateless, no CSRF)
  - Receives updates from Telegram; logs `chat_id` for initial recipient setup.
  - Secret validated against `config('telegram.webhook_secret')`.
- Booking Telegram notify: `POST /admin/prenotazioni/{id}/notify-telegram` (requires `manage_bookings`)
  - Sends booking summary, including all online check-in guest fields, only to users with a non-null `telegram_chat_id` and `telegram_notifications_enabled = true`.
  - On success updates `Booking.telegram_notified_at` and returns JSON `{"sent": true|false}`.

# Domain invariants
- Reviews are managed from each booking detail page by users with `manage_reviews`; the standalone review list is removed.
- Guest reviews use `GET /review/{token}` and `POST /review/{token}/confirm` with a booking-bound token. The token expires after `config('apartment.review.token_expiry_days')` days after checkout, rejects canceled bookings, and supports a confirmed edit flow. Every guest submission stores one locale, deletes previous translations, and sets `is_active = false` for manual review.
  Admin users with `manage_reviews` can always open the protected create/edit review form from step 5, regardless of the guest token expiry; only the guest-facing form, request email, and public form preview are limited by the active review window.
  `rating` is an integer from 1 to 10. Each `review_translations` row may also
  contain optional `liked_text` and `disliked_text`; the main review text is
  required in Italian and uses the existing locale -> English -> Italian
  fallback. The review itself may also contain an optional `private_comment`
  entered by the guest; it is stored as a single non-localized field, is never
  rendered publicly, and is available only in the protected review form for
  authorized admin users. Editing the public review replaces translations but
  preserves this private comment unless the guest changes it.
- Canceled booking state is `canceled_at != null`.
- Canceled bookings do not block public availability.
- Booking restore is allowed only when no conflicts exist with active bookings or manual blocks.
- Physical booking deletion removes linked `availability_block`.
- Pricing is recurring by month/day by default (no year). A `pricing_rules.year` override makes a rule apply to one specific calendar year only, taking priority over recurring rules for that year (used for movable holidays — see "Movable holiday pricing" below).

# Service map
- `BookingCreationService`: creates booking + person + availability block from normalized data (Interhome import). Guest matching (`findOrCreatePerson()`/`previewMatch()`: email → phone → exact first+last name → else create) is the single source of truth for "find or create this guest" — reused by the import flow and by `BookingRequestController::confirm()`, never duplicated. Matching queries include soft-deleted `Person` rows (`withTrashed()`) and `findOrCreatePerson()` restores a matched trashed person: `people.email`/`people.phone` have plain unique DB constraints not scoped to `deleted_at`, so a trashed person would otherwise cause a duplicate-entry SQL error on the next attempt to reuse that email/phone.

## The 3 places that create a `Booking` — keep them in sync
A `Booking` row is created from 3 different call sites, and it's easy to add a rule to one and forget the others:
1. `Admin\BookingController::store()` — "nuova prenotazione" admin form
2. `Admin\BookingRequestController::confirm()` — "Accetta" button on a pending guest request
3. `BookingCreationService::createFromParsed()` — Interhome PDF import

**Rule of thumb**: any business rule that must apply to *every* new booking (defaults, invariants, side effects) belongs in `Booking::booted()` (a `static::creating(...)` / `static::created(...)` listener on the model), NOT duplicated in each controller/service above. Before adding "apply X when a booking is created" logic to a controller, search for `Booking::create(` across the repo to see how many places would need the same fix.

Example: the tax-declaration flag defaults below used to live only in `BookingController::store()` — accepting a request or importing a PDF silently produced bookings with `income_tax`/`cleaning_tax`/etc. at the DB column default (`false`) instead of the configured default. Fixed by moving the defaulting into `Booking::booted()`.
- `PricingQuoteService`: single pricing engine (public quote + admin simulator).
- `InterhomePdfBookingParser`: parses Interhome PDFs into normalized records.
- `TelegramService`: sends Telegram messages via Bot API (`sendMessage`, `sendToAllRecipients`). Recipients require both `users.telegram_chat_id` and `users.telegram_notifications_enabled`.
- `TelegramBookingMessageBuilder`: formats the booking summary and all guest check-in fields for Telegram. Arrival reminders include the guest block; departure reminders remain concise.

# Movable holiday pricing (Easter/Pentecost)
- Problem: `pricing_rules` are recurring by month/day, but Easter/Pentecost shift every year (lunar calendar) and can't be expressed as a fixed recurring window.
- Fix: `pricing_rules.year` (nullable). When set, the rule matches only that year and outranks recurring rules for it (`PricingQuoteService::matchesRule` + priority sort).
- **Easter is fully automatic**: `App\Console\Commands\SyncEasterPricingRule` (`php artisan pricing:sync-easter {year?}`) computes the real Easter Sunday date (Meeus/Jones/Butcher algorithm) and upserts a `year`-specific "Pasqua {year}" rule (default window: Easter Sunday −3/+2 days). Idempotent — matches by `year` + `note LIKE 'Pasqua %'`. Scheduled every 1st November for the following year (see Scheduled jobs below). No manual action needed unless the price or window width should change (`--price`, `--days-before`, `--days-after` options).
- **Pentecost/Pfingstferien is NOT automatic**: the discount period tracked (`note` mentions "Vacanze Scuole Germania") follows German school holiday calendars, which vary per Bundesland and are not a fixed offset from Easter. This rule must be reviewed/updated manually every year (set a new `year`-specific row with the correct dates once the relevant Land's school calendar is published).

# Scheduled jobs (`routes/console.php`)
| Command | Schedule | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `SendTelegramBookingReminders --type=checkin` | daily at `apartment.booking.checkin_time` | Arrival reminders |
| `SendTelegramBookingReminders --type=checkout` | daily at `apartment.booking.checkout_time` | Departure reminders |
| `SyncEasterPricingRule` (`pricing:sync-easter`) | yearly, Nov 1st 03:00 | Creates/updates next year's Easter pricing rule |

# Configuration and precedence
- Source of truth booking defaults: `config/apartment.php`.
- Public check-in lead time comes from `apartment.booking.min_booking_lead_days`
  (default 7) and is enforced on both quote and availability request endpoints.
- `settings` DB only for:
  - `booking_mode`
  - `booking_external_url`
- Do not use `settings` for `min_nights`, `max_nights`, `cleaning_fee`, `linen_fee_per_person`, `hide_price_from`.
- `PricingQuoteService::calculate()` signature: `(string $checkin, string $checkout, int $guests = 1)`. Returns: `{available, nights, guests, stay_cents, cleaning_cents, linen_cents, total_cents, avg_per_night_cents}`. No discount logic.

# Quick checklist before changing backend
1. Confirm impacted endpoints/routes (`routes/web.php`, `routes/admin.php`).
2. Keep controllers thin; keep logic in services/models.
3. Verify side effects on availability, pricing, and PDF import.
4. Update impacted docs in the same change set.

# Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

## Roles
| Slug | Description |
|---|---|
| `super_admin` | Full access to all features |
| `host_owner` | Full access except `manage_users` and `import_pdf` |
| `host_keeper` | Viewer only: calendar, bookings (no `income_amount`), guests |

Host keeper users can store an optional `phone` contact in the admin user form. The payment-received guest email includes this number, when present, alongside the host keeper email.

Roles are predefined in `RoleSeeder` — not dynamically created via UI.

## Permissions
| Slug | Protects |
|---|---|
| `view_bookings` | Lista e dettaglio prenotazioni (read-only, no `income_amount`) |
| `manage_bookings` | Crea/modifica/elimina/cancella prenotazioni |
| `import_pdf` | Importa prenotazioni da PDF Interhome |
| `view_people` | Lista e dettaglio ospiti (read-only) |
| `manage_people` | Crea/modifica/elimina ospiti |
| `view_calendar` | Visualizza calendario |
| `manage_calendar` | Crea/elimina blocchi disponibilità |
| `view_accounting` | Accesso contabilità, campo `income_amount`, widget dashboard |
| `manage_pricing` | Prezzi e sconti soggiorno |
| `manage_settings` | Impostazioni generali |
| `manage_newsletter` | Newsletter |
| `manage_users` | Gestione utenti **(non delegabile via override)** |

## How to check permissions in code
```php
// Blade
@if(auth()->user()->hasPermission('view_accounting'))

// PHP
$user->isSuperAdmin();              // true if role is super_admin
$user->hasPermission('manage_pricing'); // checks role + per-user overrides
```

Do **not** override Laravel's `can()` method. Use `hasPermission()` and `isSuperAdmin()` exclusively for admin authorization.

## How authorization is enforced
- **Route level**: `permission:<slug>` middleware on route groups in `routes/admin.php`
- **View level**: `@if(auth()->user()->hasPermission(...))` Blade conditionals
- Controllers do NOT contain authorization checks — they stay focused on business logic.

## Data model
- `users.role_id` → FK to `roles`
- `roles.telegram_notifications_enabled` → default Telegram recipient state for the role
- `users.telegram_notifications_enabled` → effective per-user Telegram recipient state; changing a user's role resets it to the new role default
- `role_permissions` pivot → role's default permissions
- `user_permissions` pivot → per-user overrides (additive; `manage_users` is excluded from overrides)

## Adding a new role or permission
1. Add to `PermissionSeeder` / `RoleSeeder`
2. Add `permission:<slug>` middleware to the relevant route group in `routes/admin.php`
3. Add `@if(auth()->user()->hasPermission(...))` in affected Blade templates

# Tax Declaration (Dichiarazione dei redditi)

## Controller
`TaxDeclarationController@index` — `GET /admin/dichiarazione-redditi?year=YYYY`
- Protected by `permission:view_accounting` middleware (same group as Contabilità).
- Named route: `admin.tax-declaration.index`.

## Query logic
- Booking income: flagged with `income_tax = true`, paid (`income_paid = true`), date from `COALESCE(income_paid_at, checkout)`.
- Booking parking: flagged with `parking_tax = true`, paid (`parking_paid = true`), date from `COALESCE(parking_paid_at, checkout)`.
- Booking cleaning/linen: flagged with `cleaning_tax`/`linen_tax = true`, paid, date from `COALESCE(services_paid_at, checkout)`.
- `financial_entries`: flagged with `tax_declaration = true`, any type; `entry_date` used for year assignment.

# Financial Attachments

Polymorphic file attachments for financial movements. Documents (invoices, receipts, etc.) can be attached to either a `FinancialEntry` or a `Booking`.

## Endpoints (all under `permission:view_accounting`)
- `POST   /admin/allegati/{type}/{id}` — upload a file (`type` = `entry` | `booking`)
- `GET    /admin/allegati/{attachment}/download` — serve file download (private disk)
- `DELETE /admin/allegati/{attachment}` — delete file + DB record

## Storage
- Private disk (`local`): files saved to `storage/app/private/finance-attachments/{type}s/{id}/{uuid}.{ext}`
- Never publicly accessible; served only via authenticated controller
- Accepted: PDF, JPG, PNG, DOC, DOCX, XLS, XLSX — max 10 MB

## Model & relations
- `FinancialAttachment` model with `morphTo('attachable')`
- `FinancialEntry` and `Booking` both have `morphMany(FinancialAttachment::class, 'attachable')`
- Delete attachment → physically removes file from disk before deleting DB record

## UX
- In `finance/index`: each movement row has a 📎 icon button; count shown if > 0; clicking opens a native `<dialog>` modal with list + upload form
- In `finance/form` (edit only): attachment section rendered below the main form card
- Only flagged+paid items count toward totals (cash-basis). Flagged+unpaid items appear in the table with "Da pagare" status.

## Config defaults
`config/finance.php` key `tax_declaration_defaults`: `income`, `cleaning`, `linen` default `true`; `parking` defaults `false`.
Applied centrally in `Booking::booted()` (a `static::creating()` listener that fills any of the 4 flags left `null` with the config default) — see "The 3 places that create a `Booking`" above. This guarantees the admin form, request confirmation, and PDF import all get the same defaults, since the `bookings` table columns themselves default to `false`. Also applied via migration (one-off) for existing rows.

